5b255d9d-9741-4b95-8cf0-0592bf5bda1f	bc172cd8-3cb9-46b4-ab5f-34a66a48902c	3ed9965f-ae3f-49e9-b87d-67fa636c568c	MCQ	MEDIUM	While conducting a pre-flight inspection, a technician notices that the journey log is incomplete, missing entries of recent maintenance performed. What is the technician's best course of action?	{"Proceed with the flight as long as the aircraft appears airworthy.","Inform the pilot and document the observation in the journey log.","Complete the missing entries themselves to avoid delays.","Contact the maintenance manager for further instructions."}	Inform the pilot and document the observation in the journey log.	According to CAR 605.86, the journey log must accurately reflect all maintenance performed, and it is essential for flight safety that discrepancies are reported. Documenting the issue helps maintain compliance with record-keeping requirements.	APPROVED	generated-backend:tp14038e-full-2026-05-08	2026-05-08 15:42:23.479	2026-05-08 16:37:02.938	4207ec2b-b214-4ab9-b012-c4616f5322f3	Selon la RAC 605.86, le journal de bord doit refléter fidèlement toute la maintenance effectuée.	["Procéder au vol tant que l'avion semble navigable.","Informer le pilote et documenter l'observation dans le journal de bord.","Remplir les inscriptions manquantes soi-même pour éviter les retards.","Contacter le responsable de maintenance pour des instructions."]	Lors d'une inspection pré-vol, un technicien remarque que le journal de bord est incomplet. Quelle est la meilleure marche à suivre ?
