be1826f7-1fc5-4010-8ff3-e86fb89af844	bc172cd8-3cb9-46b4-ab5f-34a66a48902c	3ed9965f-ae3f-49e9-b87d-67fa636c568c	MCQ	EASY	A technician discovers an incorrect torque setting on a critical aircraft component after maintenance has been performed. What is the correct procedure to follow?	{"Document the torque setting and wait for the next scheduled maintenance.","Re-torque the component to the correct specification and document the action.","Leave the component as is, as the maintenance is already completed.","Notify the pilot and let them decide on the action."}	Re-torque the component to the correct specification and document the action.	CAR 571.10 requires that all maintenance must meet the manufacturer’s specifications, including torque settings, and any corrective actions must be documented.	APPROVED	generated-backend:tp14038e-full-2026-05-08	2026-05-08 15:43:06.739	2026-05-08 16:37:02.938	4207ec2b-b214-4ab9-b012-c4616f5322f3	La RAC 571.10 exige que toute maintenance réponde aux spécifications du fabricant.	["Documenter et attendre la prochaine maintenance.","Re-sererrer à la spécification correcte et documenter.","Laisser le composant tel quel.","Informer le pilote."]	Un technicien découvre un couple incorrect sur un composant critique après maintenance. Procédure correcte ?
