4f9e94d6-2a3b-47d6-8eab-1269d6ca1f9a	dad311a9-dad8-4d99-b7a5-839bbb8b1d28	684416e8-047c-4079-882b-795d0db338b3	MCQ	EASY	A technician is tasked with inspecting the aircraft's electrical system for signs of corrosion. Which of the following areas should be prioritized during the inspection?	{"Connectors and terminals exposed to moisture.","Circuit breakers and fuses.","Wiring insulation and sheathing.","Battery compartments and battery leads."}	Connectors and terminals exposed to moisture.	Connectors and terminals are critical points in the electrical system where corrosion can lead to significant failures. Moisture exposure increases the risk of corrosion, making these areas the priority during inspections, in accordance with AC 43.13.	APPROVED	generated-backend:tp14038e-full-2026-05-08	2026-05-08 15:43:46.541	2026-05-08 16:37:02.938	4207ec2b-b214-4ab9-b012-c4616f5322f3	Connecteurs et bornes exposés à l'humidité sont prioritaires selon l'AC 43.13.	["Connecteurs et bornes exposés à l'humidité.","Disjoncteurs et fusibles.","Isolation du câblage.","Compartiments de batterie."]	Inspection du système électrique pour corrosion. Zone à prioriser ?
